      <h1>How to Write Midjourney Prompts in 2026 (The 7-Pattern Framework)</h1>
      <p class="lede">Stop guessing. The 7 Midjourney prompt patterns that consistently produce publishable images - with 20 real before/after examples and the exact prompts you can copy.</p>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-calendar"></i> 2026-06-10</span>
        <span class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-clock"></i> 14 min read</span>
        <span class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-user"></i> Sofia Reyes, Product Designer</span>
      </div>
    </header>
      <img src="/images/blog/how-to-write-prompts-for-midjourney-2026/hero.jpg" alt="How to Write Midjourney Prompts in 2026 (The 7-Pattern Framework)" style="width:100%;border-radius:12px;margin:24px 0;" loading="eager" />

    <section class="blog-content">
      <p>After generating 500+ Midjourney images for client work in 2026, I can tell you the difference between a good image and a great one is almost never the model - it is the prompt. Midjourney v7 is the most capable image model in the world for aesthetic quality, but it cannot read your mind. The 7 patterns below are the ones that consistently produce publishable output, with 20 real before/after examples to show the difference.</p>

      
      <Chart type="timeline" title="Learning Path" data={[
        {date: "Week 1", title: "Getting Started", description: "Learn the basics and set up."},
        {date: "Week 2", title: "Core Features", description: "Master main features through practice."},
        {date: "Week 3", title: "Advanced", description: "Explore advanced workflows."},
